{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implemented — change 1666 pushed for review\n\nBase: origin/main @ cc69cc1179. Worktree: nyala-unbind-leak. Commit e262fe169b.\n\n### Fix 1 — `unbind()` is self-contained (`binding_store.py:426`)\n\nGating the reverse pop on the forward entry's `jira_key` made cleanup of one index depend\non the other, which the method had just destroyed. The keyed pop stays as an O(1) fast path;\na sweep then clears any residual `reverse[K] == local_id`.\n\nRED confirmed before the fix: `test_unbind_clears_reverse_when_forward_entry_lost_its_jira_key`\nand `test_unbind_clears_reverse_when_forward_entry_is_already_gone` both failed on\ncc69cc1179 (`assert 'REB-411' not in {'REB-411': 'local-2'}`); the three regression cells in\nthe same file passed before and after.\n\n### Fix 2 — `rebar bridge fsck --repair`\n\nNew module `src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py` (229 LOC). `bridge_fsck.main()` gains the\nflag and delegates; the audit functions are untouched, so the L9 read-only boundary holds.\n\n**Design note (deviation from the plan, for the better):** the plan assumed the verb might\nneed new `BindingStore` surface. It does not. Once fix 1 lands, `unbind(local_id)` clears a\n*stranded* reverse key too — the forward pop no-ops and the sweep does the work — so the\nprune is expressible through the existing public API. The repair module never touches\n`_data` (it uses `all_bindings()`, `is_bound()`, `get_local_id()`), and `binding_store.py`\nstayed under the 800-LOC cap at **798**, which adding a method there would have blown.\n\nThe two fixes are coupled by test, not just narrative: without fix 1 the prune's guard 4\ncatches the residual key and refuses with exit 1, so every prune happy-path cell fails.\n\nFour guards, all **pre-write** (verification runs in memory before `save()`, so a refusal\nleaves the file byte-identical):\n1. every `store_integrity` finding must be kind `reverse_missing_forward`;\n2. no orphan key may appear in `bindings-retired.json`;\n3. no orphan may have gained a forward binding since the audit;\n4. the forward map must be unchanged and no orphan may remain.\n\nThe finding set comes from `audit_store_integrity()`, never a re-derivation — the same\nrepair-consumes-the-detector discipline `tracker_maintenance.py:93` uses. Durable audit\nlands in the tracker's **git dir** (`rebar-bridge-repair-audit.jsonl`), asserted by test not\nto appear in the worktree. Exit codes: 0 healed/no-op, 1 refused, 2 operational.\n\nI dropped the planned `--force` break-glass: every guard is a refusal an operator resolves\nby fixing the store, so a bypass would only enable the deletion the guards exist to prevent.\n\n### Gates (worktree venv)\n\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean.\n- `pytest tests/scripts/bridge tests/unit/rebar_reconciler` — **2501 passed**.\n- 9 new prune cells + 5 new unbind cells.\n- Module size: `binding_store.py` 798/800, `bridge_repair.py` 229, `bridge_fsck.py` 684.\n- `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` reports no drift.\n\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1666"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786560277429590001,"uuid":"e54ddce4-f89a-43ac-8464-284d582f6809"}